A||||6||308||Help!!  My cruz control doesn't work||||5||
Z||000000||308||08-23-2001||12:24 AM||||I have an 87 GT, witht he 2.8 it only has 51,000 miles on it, The guy I got it from said the cruz never worked, anyone have any idea of some basic checks or if there is a common thing that goes out.  The only thing I noticed is that around the cruz unit it looks like a spot where a vac. line might go, we'll if anyone can help, please let me know, Larry||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||08-23-2001||07:46 AM||||Automatic or stick?<BR>For a stick there are two switches, one on the clutch and another on the brake pedal. Check these to insure they are closed when the pedal is up, if either are open the cruise will not engauge. For an auto, just a brake switch.<BR>What you may be seeing in back where a vac line may go, if it points toward the passenger side of car it is a vent to atmosphere.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierohoho||08-23-2001||10:16 AM||||The first thing to check would be the cruise stalk, that is basically the turn signal handle. <P>You can get a new one from Rodney Dickman, check his web site.<P>Or you could hit the junk yard and try to pickup a couple there, one may be good. <P>The stalk pulls straight out of the column with moderate presure and the only wire attached to it runs down to the plug under the dash. <P>When you pull the wire through the column tie a string to it to aid in pulling the new wire through. <P>If thats not the problem then we'll go from there. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pennockpic.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Leadfoot||08-23-2001||10:21 AM||||It could also be the vac canister (looks like a coffee can) has a broken seam.  Take it off, submerge it under water, and blow air into the vac ports.  If you see bubbles then the can is bad.  You can by a plastic replacement from napa.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jim Jimenez||08-24-2001||01:41 AM||||About that vacuum canister. You are not going to believe this, but if you need a exact replacement one, check out a 1980's FORD pickup, you have to exchange the mounting bracket with yours, and both the inlet and outlet nipples are the same size, but it is a dead ringer and the concours judges will never know. Original part is discontinued from GM.||||reg||12
Z||000005||Old Lar||08-24-2001||08:30 AM||||The vaccuum bellows right above the "coffee" can may be leaking also.  That was my problem. Cruise would work for a while and shut off, new stalk didn't help.||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfixit58||08-24-2001||09:22 AM||||Try reading this. It outlines a very good procedure for troubleshooting the cruise control system in a Fiero. It worked for me.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/diag.cruise-control.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/diag.cruise-control.html</A> <P>Good Luck,<P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||3
